spec: S06-07, S06-08

Tokens: the owner mints for another Member (name, expiry) — printed once like `member add` —
and lists that Member's; a Member mints and lists their own (TTY parity, JSON). Revoking by id
needs the id, which trycmd cannot capture (`crates/annotary/tests/cli_access.rs` covers
mint → revoke → 401 with the real binary; `token-mint-tty.toml` beside this file is the TTY
form). Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan token mint --member linter --name ci --expires 30d
token minted for @linter "ci" (id [..], expires [..])
Token (shown once):
ANNOTARY_TOKEN=ant_[..]

$ annotary -p rowan token list --member linter
@linter	member add	[..]	-	-	[..]
@linter	ci	[..]	-	[..]-[..]-[..]	[..]

$ annotary -p rowan token list --member linter --json name,member,expires,status
[{"name":"member add","member":"linter","status":"active"},{"name":"ci","member":"linter","expires":"[..]T[..]Z","status":"active"}]

$ annotary -p agent token mint --name laptop
token minted for @scribe "laptop" (id [..])
Token (shown once):
ANNOTARY_TOKEN=ant_[..]

$ annotary -p agent token mint --json member,name,expires
token minted for @scribe (id [..])
Token (shown once):
{"member":"scribe"}

$ annotary -p agent token list
@scribe	member add	[..]	[..]	-	[..]
@scribe	laptop	[..]	-	-	[..]
@scribe	-	[..]	-	-	[..]

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary -p agent token list --no-color
MEMBER   NAME        CREATED  LAST USED  EXPIRES  ID
@scribe  member add  [..]
@scribe  laptop      [..]
@scribe  -           [..]

$ annotary -p agent token list --json name,status
[{"name":"member add","status":"active"},{"name":"laptop","status":"active"},{"status":"active"}]

```
